
✅✅✅✅✅✅✅✅✅✅ Connection Pooling ✅✅✅✅✅✅✅✅✅✅

Creating a DB connection is expensive:
TCP connection setup
Authentication
Session initialization
Memory allocation on DB

Opening a new connection for every request adds latency and increases DB load.

Databases also have limited connections:
PostgreSQL default ≈ 100
MySQL default ≈ 151

During traffic spikes, applications can exhaust DB connections and cause failures.

Connection Pooling
Instead of creating new connections repeatedly, applications reuse existing DB connections.

Flow:
Server asks pool for a connection
Pool provides an idle connection
Query executes
Connection returns to pool instead of closing

This avoids repeated connection setup overhead and improves performance.

Types
Internal Pooling
Pooling inside application instances.
Problem:
3 app instances × 150 pool size = 450 DB connections

Scaling app servers increases total DB connections rapidly.

External Pooling
Use a dedicated pooler like PgBouncer.
App Servers -> PgBouncer -> Database
All app instances share a centralized pool, reducing DB connection pressure and handling spikes more efficiently.

const mysql = require("mysql2/promise");
const pool = mysql.createPool({
  host: "localhost",
  user: "root",
  password: "password",
  database: "app_db",

  waitForConnections: true,

  // maxConnections
  connectionLimit: 100,

  // maxIdle
  maxIdle: 10,

  // idleTimeout
  idleTimeout: 30000,

  // connectionTimeout
  connectTimeout: 5000
});

connectionLimit (maxConnections)
Maximum DB connections pool can create.
connectionLimit: 100

If all are busy:
requests wait
or fail after timeout

Too high → DB overload
Too low → request queueing

maxIdle
Maximum idle connections kept open.
maxIdle: 10
Reuses existing connections instead of reopening TCP/auth/session repeatedly.

Too high → wasted DB resources
Too low → reconnect overhead

idleTimeout
How long idle connections stay open.
idleTimeout: 30000
Unused connections are closed after 30s.

connectTimeout
Maximum wait time while establishing DB connection.
connectTimeout: 5000
Prevents requests hanging forever during DB/network issues.
